atterns that we  can see with Luffy or Big Mama the red  color scheme of the road Pony glyphs  might also be related to the red we see  displayed when two uses of conquerors  haki clash now while it might be easy to  say that the Pony glyphs color scheme is  related to that of armament haki I'm  well aware of the fact that the color  aspect of hockey is still a little bit  controversial  it is not clear in many cases if it is a  design choice or intentional yet we know  that the kanji for color is explicitly  part of the full description for hockey  and is being used in the manga as well  in my opinion since armament can also be  translated as the color of arms it might  very well serve as a legitimate fourth  argument here all in all I think that  the theory that the Pony glyphs are made  using haki infusion has some very solid  arguments that would explain a lot of  the mystery surrounding them and it  would also bring even more importance to  the role of armament haki in this arc  now as a conclusion I would like to give  you guys a few questions to ponder upon  off  watching this video do you think he  could break a pony glyph was strong  enough haki how many people would have  worked on creating a pony to live in the  first place and how good were they with  hockey what other objects might be  infused with hockey in the one-piece  world and finally do you have any  additional arguments for or against his  theory share your thoughts and ideas in  the comments below if you like this  video don't forget to like share and  subscribe to be notified for any future  content of mine or dislike don't share  and unsubscribe it's a free world people  I hope to see you around next time and  until then have a great week  you  [Music]

